listing:   run.sh (step ring_trace)
toolchain: QEMU emulator version 8.2.2 (Debian 1:8.2.2+ds-0ubuntu1.18); TShark (Wireshark) 4.2.2 (Git v4.2.2 packaged as 4.2.2-1.1build3).
command:   qemu-system-x86_64 -machine q35 -nodefaults -display none -serial none -monitor none -no-reboot -boot order=n -netdev user,id=n0 -device e1000e,netdev=n0,mac=52:54:00:12:34:56 -object filter-dump,id=f1,netdev=n0,file=ring.pcap -trace e1000e_core_write -trace e1000e_rx_set_rdt -trace e1000e_tx_descr -trace e1000e_rx_descr -trace e1000e_rx_written_to_guest -trace e1000e_irq_set -trace e1000e_link_status -D trace.txt  (stopped after 20 s by timeout)
date:      2026-10-09T19:17:19Z
machine:   Linux x86_64 (cloud build container; QEMU with TCG, no KVM)
exit code: 124
hardware:  emulated NICs only (QEMU device models); untested on a physical NIC
note:      exit code 124 is expected: QEMU was stopped by the 20 s time limit after the boot ROM gave up
